  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Scattered showers and thunderstorms tonight and again \nSaturday afternoon/evening will bring localized threat for \ngusty wind, and rain heavy enough to increase the chance for \nlocalized flash flooding.\n\nAdditional SHRA/TSRA are expected through the night, mainly over\nthe next 2 hrs - progressing east from current radar positions,\nand then again before sunrise in the west. Some of the cells\nacross nrn PA do have heavy rain in them, and recent rainfall\nhas made lower FFGs there than many places in the CWA. We will\ncontinue to keep an eye out for these cells as the current\nclustering and cell movements make it seem like training is\nstarting to occur. \n\nThe rain/showers arriving in the west before morning will be at\na time which would help stabilize things over the NW half or\nmore of the CWA on Sat as rain/clouds keep the CAPEs low over a\ngood portion of the area. However, the SE still has the best\nchance for deep convection. SPC outlook is for a MRGL risk of\nSVR gusts in that area. It is conditional depending on the\namount of clouds/stabilization present there in prime time.\nHeavy rain is still a possibility, too, but perhaps less than\nFriday.",
